<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish July industrial output rises 1.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Irish July industrial output rises 1.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish industrial production rose a seasonally-adjusted 1.2 percent in July and was up 8.8 percent year-on-year Central Statistics Office (CSO) data showed on Friday.  </p>
<p>Manufacturing production rose/fell x.x percent in July and was up 8.6 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>		    Manufacturing  Transportable    All industries</p>
<p>			   (PERCENTAGE CHANGE - MONTH ON MONTH)</p>
<p> Latest month	+3.9		+0.3		 +1.2</p>
<p> Previous month    -0.9		+3.2		 +2.0</p>
<p>			   (PERCENTAGE CHANGE - YEAR ON YEAR)</p>
<p> Latest month	+8.6		+9.1		 +8.8</p>
<p> Previous month    +15.0	     +13.7		+13.1</p>
<p>					(INDEX BASE 1985)</p>
<p> Latest month	 272.2	    268.1		255.3</p>
<p> Previous month     261.9	    267.2		252.3</p>
<p> Year ago month     250.6	    245.6		234.7</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom 353 1 660 3377</p>
